<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>AI Act standards map</title>
<link rel="icon" href="data:,">
<meta name="description" content="Which AI Act high-risk requirements are covered by harmonised standards, and when.">
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega@5.30.0" integrity="sha384-em7CHpJd+SsMugVFf6TY7AKQcLWMcbPhD84hmNK8o6WFDkK+2uHSUQRVQV1/w827" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-lite@5.21.0" integrity="sha384-GhkD6ks9/zgY1m5EFOUZWz/vMVMUFF/92DL61RZc+B42J8osL+jNufKv68bNHHZ2" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-embed@6.26.0" integrity="sha384-TqXb8su49m5OnEpKGO8m+VrgHesrUxyP22HgpXi4hnh1Hm43dXroiSYemNf5D8lv" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
<style>
  :root { --ink:#1b1b1b; --muted:#5b5b5b; --line:#d9d9d9; --hair:#ececec; --bg:#ffffff; --accent:#1f4e79;
          --uncovered:#9b1c1c; --in-progress:#8a5a00; --published:#1f4e79; --harmonised:#1e6b3a; }
  ::selection { background:#d6e4f2; color:var(--ink); }
  body { margin:0; font:16px/1.55 system-ui, sans-serif; color:var(--ink); background:var(--bg);
         -webkit-text-size-adjust:100%; }
  main { max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 20px 72px; }
  h1 { font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -.015em; margin: 0 0 12px; text-wrap: balance; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; line-height: 1.25; letter-spacing: -.01em; margin: 64px 0 8px; padding-top: 20px;
       border-top: 1px solid var(--ink); text-wrap: balance; }
  p, li { max-width: 72ch; }
  p { margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .meta, footer { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; }
  code { font-size: .9em; }
  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin: 20px 0 12px; }
  .table-wrap:focus-visible, a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: .93rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 8px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair); vertical-align: top; }
  th:first-child, td:first-child { padding-left: 0; } th:last-child, td:last-child { padding-right: 0; }
  thead th { font-size: .8rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); vertical-align: bottom;
             border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink); }
  thead th span { display: block; font-weight: 400; }
  .num { text-align: right; } .nowrap { white-space: nowrap; }
  #coverage-table { min-width: 620px; } #timeline-table { min-width: 760px; }
  .status { white-space: nowrap; font-weight: 500; }
  .status::before { content: ""; display: inline-block; width: .6em; height: .6em; margin-right: .5em;
                    background: currentColor; }
  .status-uncovered, .late { color: var(--uncovered); } .status-in_progress, .passed { color: var(--in-progress); }
  .status-published { color: var(--published); } .status-harmonised { color: var(--harmonised); }
  .unknown { color: var(--muted); }
  .chart { width: 100%; margin: 12px 0 0; }
  a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: .16em; }
  a:hover { text-decoration-thickness: 2px; }
  ul { padding-left: 1.1em; } li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  footer { margin-top: 64px; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    main { padding: 28px 16px 56px; } h1 { font-size: 1.65rem; } h2 { margin-top: 48px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<h1>AI Act standards map</h1>
<p class="meta">Coverage of the high-risk requirements (Articles 8–15 of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689) by the harmonised standards requested from CEN-CENELEC JTC 21. As of {{ today }}. Version {{ version }}.</p>
<p>The project <strong>describes, it does not interpret</strong>: every row cites a public source by article and paragraph, and judgements are marked as such in a <code>note</code> column. Only public sources are used.</p>

<h2>Coverage by requirement</h2>
<div id="coverage" class="chart"></div>
<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Coverage by requirement, table">
<table id="coverage-table">
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Article</th><th scope="col">Requirement</th><th scope="col" class="num">Deliverables</th><th scope="col" class="num">Work items</th><th scope="col" class="num">At enquiry or later</th><th scope="col" class="num">Published</th><th scope="col" class="num">Cited in OJEU</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for r in coverage %}
<tr><td>{{ r.article }}</td><td>{{ r.title }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.n_deliverables }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.n_work_items }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.n_at_enquiry_or_later }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.n_published }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.n_harmonised }}</td><td class="status status-{{ r.status }}">{{ r.status.replace('_',' ') }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% for n in coverage_notes %}
<p class="meta">Article {{ n.article }} (via {{ n.deliverable_id }}): {{ n.note }}</p>
{% endfor %}

<h2>Work items against the application dates</h2>
<div id="timeline" class="chart"></div>
<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Work items against the application dates, table">
<table id="timeline-table">
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Work item</th><th scope="col">Title</th><th scope="col">Deliverable</th><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">Target publication</th>{% for d in deadlines %}<th scope="col" class="num">Days from target to {{ d.deadline_id }}<span>{{ d.deadline_date }}</span></th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for t in items %}
<tr><td class="nowrap">{{ t.wi_ref }}</td><td>{{ t.title }}</td><td>{{ t.deliverable_id }}</td><td>{{ t.stage_code }} {{ t.stage_name }}</td><td class="nowrap">{{ t.target_pub_date or '—' }}</td>{% for d in deadlines %}{% set c = t.days.get(d.deadline_id) %}{% if not c %}<td class="num unknown">—</td>{% elif c.days != '' %}<td class="num{{ ' late' if c.late == 'true' }}">{{ c.days }}</td>{% elif c.late == 'target_passed' %}<td class="num passed">target date passed</td>{% else %}<td class="num unknown">unknown</td>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p class="meta">Days are counted from the target publication date to the deadline; a negative number means the target falls after the deadline.</p>
{% for d in deadlines %}
<p class="meta">{{ d.deadline_id }} ({{ d.deadline_date }}){% if d.scope %}: {{ d.scope }}{% endif %}</p>
{% endfor %}

<h2>Data and method</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Curated tables: {% for name in curated_files %}<a href="data/{{ name }}">{{ name }}</a>{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}</li>
  <li>Derived tables: <a href="data/coverage_by_requirement.csv">coverage_by_requirement.csv</a>, <a href="data/timeline.csv">timeline.csv</a>{% if "standards_history.csv" in other_files %}, <a href="data/standards_history.csv">standards_history.csv</a>{% endif %}</li>
{% if "adoption.csv" in other_files %}
  <li>Adoption data: <a href="data/adoption.csv">adoption.csv</a>{% if lineage %} ({{ lineage.rows }} rows, retrieved {{ lineage.retrieved_at }}, SHA-256 {{ lineage.sha256[:12] }}…). Source: Eurostat, <code>isoc_eb_ain2</code>{% endif %}</li>
{% endif %}
  <li><a href="quality.md">Quality note</a> · <a href="{{ repo_url }}/blob/main/docs/methodology.md">Methodology</a> · <a href="{{ repo_url }}">Repository</a></li>
</ul>

<footer>
<p>Data: CC BY 4.0. Code: MIT. Eurostat data: Source: Eurostat. Standards metadata are facts from public CEN-CENELEC pages; no standard text is reproduced. This is a personal project and does not represent any employer.</p>
</footer>
</main>
<script>
  vegaEmbed("#coverage", {{ specs.coverage | tojson }}, {actions: false});
  vegaEmbed("#timeline", {{ specs.timeline | tojson }}, {actions: false});
</script>
</body>
</html>
